    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The suite has one runnable test class (`AcceptanceTest`), which now goes green, and the rest are the abstract base and a helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end, following the OfficeFloor/DTO conventions already used for the owner's other derived fields (`displayName`, `ageBand`, `locality`, etc.).\n\n**Input & output contract** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`:\n- Added an optional `title` field to `OwnerFields` (the request), constrained by pattern `^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$` so `@Valid` rejects anything else as a 400.\n- Added a read-only `salutation` field to `Owner` (the response).\n\nThe DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`) are generated from this spec at build time, so `getTitle()`/`getSalutation()` accessors appear automatically.\n\n**Domain logic** \u2014 `Owner.java`:\n- Added a persisted `title` column (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter \u2014 it must be persisted because `salutation` is read back on a separate `GET /api/owners/{id}` request.\n- Added a derived `getSalutation()`: `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title. This is auto-mapped into `OwnerDto` by MapStruct (matching property name), like the other derived getters.\n\n**Wiring**:\n- `BuildOwner` already delegates to `ownerMapper.toOwner(request)`, which now maps `title` automatically (matching field names) \u2014 so the POST path stores it.\n- `ApplyOwner` (the PUT path) now also copies `owner.setTitle(request.getTitle())` for consistency.\n\n**Schema** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four DB scripts (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`); tests run against hsqldb.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (POST with `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, then GET expecting `salutation = \"DR who\"`) passes.\n\nI did not add `@RestController`/`@Transactional` etc.; validation stays declarative via `@Valid` in the existing `ValidateOwner` step, per the project's OfficeFloor conventions.",
